+# KLZH2 (codec 32): results
+
+Branch `review40/R01`, from release-rc3 `5071f388`. Claim `klzh-entropy-v2` of the 40-reviewer pass (reviewer R01).
+This file holds the numbers, the commands and what did not work. The format is in `src/algo/klz.h`.
+
+**What it is.** KLZH (codec 29) coded with a second entropy stage. The parse, the levels and the repeat-offset rule
+are KLZH's; only the bytes written for a parse differ. Written only with the opt-in `KOLMO_NATIVE=lz2` (zstd and
+Brotli roles map to codec 32 instead of 29). `KOLMO_NATIVE=lz` and `all` keep writing codec 29, byte for byte, and
+no default writes either.
+
+**Machine.** A shared cloud VM (4 vCPUs, x86-64 with AVX-512 and BMI2, GCC 13.3, `-O3 -march=native`), load average
+2.0 to 3.1 during every run below. **Sizes are exact. Every speed in this file is indicative only**; the timed runs
+went one at a time through the pass's `tools/measure.py`. Ratios between two coders inside one `natbench` process
+are steadier than MB/s, and still move by several percent between runs.
+
+**Data.** Silesia (12 files, 211,938,580 bytes) and `enwik8_10m` (the first 10,000,000 bytes of enwik8): 221,938,580
+bytes. Every block of every run was decoded and compared.
+
